  by: agent  # 7fd7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7fd7
  clock: 2  # 7fd7
  nonce: 7fd7  # 7fd7
  message: "EVIDENCE 2026-09-23 from the IoPrimitive.kind concept audit (INV-zikab; write-up ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-io-primitive-kind_09232026.md).\n\n(1) A SECOND JOIN SITE THIS ITEM DOES NOT LIST: io_boundary.py:1161, the INV-nizom arm of lookup_with_module -- `if call_construct == \"method\" and len(candidates) > 1: filtered = [p for p in filtered if p.kind != \"function\"]`. It reads a `method` stamp as receiver evidence and a function row as \"cannot be a receiver call's callee\". It is LOAD-BEARING for java today: java emits a multi-candidate slot for wildcard imports (redis.clients.jedis.System,...,java.lang.System) and stamps `method` on the qualified static System.currentTimeMillis(). Re-kinding the java statics to function (the R2 reading) loses 41 classifications through this line: jedis 160->124, spring-petclinic -3, gatling -2 (21-survey A/B, d917e02282). java.yaml's note says its statics are method-kind because of the stamp, so the catalogue has been compensating for this join.\n\n(2) THIS ITEM'S STATEMENT DEFINES IoPrimitive.kind AS \"the construct of the DEFINITION\" (R1). WI-komun (done, #800) and test_associated_fn_kinds.py (INV-nular) ship the opposite reading: methods = owner supplied by a value whose type must be known. Filed as INV-zikab for the owner's decision. This item's statement should follow whichever is adopted.\n\n(3) THE STARVATION DOCSTRING'S PREMISE IS REFUTED on the main path: \"only a METHOD-construct call edge can ever match\" a method-keyed entry, yet with a definite module slot the matcher never reads kind (_qualified_rows and the module filter are kind-agnostic). Kind is consulted only at gate_named_entry and the INV-nizom arm."  # 7fd7
