  nonce: 9d7d  # 9d7d
  message: "SECOND JOIN SITE ADDRESSED (PR #1159, INV-zikab step 4): the INV-nizom arm in lookup_with_module no longer reads a method stamp as instance-receiver evidence on a slot that names ONE owner (slot_names_one_owner). It still does so on cpp's #include disjunction, where the slot really is file context. Route 1 of method_starved_modules (this item's filed site) is unchanged. This item's statement (R1, 'the construct of the DEFINITION') is rewritten in step 7 to follow ADR-0059."  # 9d7d
- op: update  # 640d
  at: '2026-09-24T00:17:31Z'  # 640d
  by: agent  # 640d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 640d
  clock: 4  # 640d
  nonce: 640d  # 640d
  set:  # 640d
    fields:  # 640d
      statement: "A satisfaction test must compare values drawn from the same vocabulary. call_construct names the SYNTAX of the call site; IoPrimitive.kind says how the primitive is reached from its row's own module (ADR-0059: method iff called on an instance of the module; function iff called on the module itself or with no owner; attribute iff read). The two overlap lexically in exactly {function, method}, but they are different axes and must not be joined by bare string equality."  # 640d
      root_cause: "MetaKeySpec declares no value vocabulary for call_construct, so the call-site side of the join has no registry to check against. The definition side has had one since ADR-0059 (io_primitive_kinds); before that it was an undeclared bare str (WI-fazad)."  # 640d
- op: discuss  # a9ca
